WEBVTT

00:00:14.844 --> 00:00:16.804 align:center line:81%
How often the average day.

00:00:16.846 --> 00:00:21.100 align:center line:79%
The average week. Do you
think about the rule of law?

00:00:21.976 --> 00:00:26.898 align:center line:79%
How the rule of law
impacts your daily life.

00:00:28.441 --> 00:00:31.110 align:center line:81%
You decide to go to the store.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.112 align:center line:81%
You need a new pair of sneakers.

00:00:33.112 --> 00:00:34.405 align:center line:81%
You jump in your car.

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:40.411 align:center line:79%
Do you come to a complete stop
at the stop sign in your neighborhood?

00:00:40.411 --> 00:00:42.497 align:center line:81%
Or do you maybe roll through it?

00:00:43.706 --> 00:00:46.751 align:center line:79%
Now you're driving on the street,
heading to the store.

00:00:46.751 --> 00:00:53.007 align:center line:79%
Do you obey all posted speed
limits or do you think to yourself, ah,

00:00:53.382 --> 00:00:57.637 align:center line:79%
I wonder how fast I can go
without getting pulled over?

00:00:58.304 --> 00:01:03.810 align:center line:79%
Okay. Fair enough. Most of us probably
engage in those daily transgressions.

00:01:04.811 --> 00:01:07.355 align:center line:81%
At the store, you park your car.

00:01:07.355 --> 00:01:12.860 align:center line:79%
Do you feed the parking meter or use
the parking app to pay for parking?

00:01:13.361 --> 00:01:17.782 align:center line:79%
Or do you just take your chances
at maybe getting a parking ticket?

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:22.036 align:center line:79%
Now you're in the store,
you're trying on those sneakers.

00:01:23.162 --> 00:01:24.997 align:center line:81%
Do you think to yourself,

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:31.629 align:center line:79%
maybe I should just run out of the store
without paying for the sneakers?

00:01:31.629 --> 00:01:33.422 align:center line:81%
Just steal them.

00:01:34.924 --> 00:01:39.971 align:center line:79%
Probably not. Right.
Well, that's the rule of law at work

00:01:40.179 --> 00:01:42.348 align:center line:81%
in your lives every day.

00:01:43.182 --> 00:01:45.977 align:center line:79%
Now, sure, it's also
your sense of morality,

00:01:45.977 --> 00:01:49.355 align:center line:79%
which is probably a product
of your upbringing.

00:01:49.689 --> 00:01:54.235 align:center line:79%
But if we didn't have laws against
speeding or stealing from stores,

00:01:54.569 --> 00:01:58.698 align:center line:79%
how different would our daily
experiences be?

00:01:59.073 --> 00:02:01.993 align:center line:81%
The rule of law is foundational

00:02:02.493 --> 00:02:06.789 align:center line:81%
to a free, fair, safe society.

00:02:08.291 --> 00:02:10.168 align:center line:81%
And when I think about the rule of law,

00:02:10.168 --> 00:02:13.838 align:center line:79%
how it impacts our lives,
how it impacts our thought processes,

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.799 align:center line:81%
both consciously and subconsciously,

00:02:17.216 --> 00:02:22.305 align:center line:79%
I always come back to my favorite
Abraham Lincoln saying,

00:02:22.722 --> 00:02:28.644 align:center line:79%
be sure to put your feet
in the right place, then stand firm.

00:02:30.146 --> 00:02:33.733 align:center line:79%
We're going to take
a big leap from speeding

00:02:33.983 --> 00:02:39.405 align:center line:79%
and shoplifting to the survival
of American democracy, right?

00:02:39.447 --> 00:02:41.324 align:center line:81%
That's a big jump.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.912 align:center line:79%
My name is Glenn Kirschner,
and I'm a rule of law guy.

00:02:45.912 --> 00:02:49.540 align:center line:79%
I started as a federal prosecutor,
as an Army JAG back in the 80s,

00:02:49.582 --> 00:02:55.213 align:center line:79%
prosecuting all manner of crimes
from death penalty to espionage cases.

00:02:55.838 --> 00:02:57.965 align:center line:81%
After six and a half years on active duty,

00:02:57.965 --> 00:03:02.011 align:center line:79%
I left the Army and I
joined the Department of Justice,

00:03:02.303 --> 00:03:06.515 align:center line:79%
specifically the US Attorney's Office
in the District of Columbia.

00:03:07.225 --> 00:03:11.354 align:center line:79%
I eventually became
chief of the homicide section

00:03:11.354 --> 00:03:13.356 align:center line:81%
at the D.C. U.S. Attorney's Office,

00:03:13.814 --> 00:03:19.445 align:center line:79%
responsible for overseeing all grand
jury investigations involving murders

00:03:19.445 --> 00:03:23.366 align:center line:79%
and all homicide prosecutions
in the courts of Washington,

00:03:23.366 --> 00:03:27.536 align:center line:79%
D.C.. After a little
over 30 years as a fed,

00:03:27.578 --> 00:03:33.668 align:center line:79%
I retired from DOJ and I began working
as an on air legal analyst

00:03:33.668 --> 00:03:40.466 align:center line:79%
for NBC news and MSNBC, discussing
and analyzing the legal issues of the day.

00:03:41.384 --> 00:03:44.845 align:center line:81%
I've also continued my rule of law work,

00:03:45.263 --> 00:03:50.851 align:center line:79%
posting daily legal analysis videos
on my YouTube channel,

00:03:50.851 --> 00:03:53.354 align:center line:81%
Justice Matters with Glenn Kirshner.

00:03:53.354 --> 00:03:58.234 align:center line:81%
Not promoting my channel, but subscribe.

00:04:00.861 --> 00:04:06.117 align:center line:79%
And every day in my 30 years
as a prosecutor

00:04:06.325 --> 00:04:10.371 align:center line:79%
and now in my professional chapter two
as a legal analyst,

00:04:10.705 --> 00:04:16.210 align:center line:79%
I try to remain keenly
aware of where I plant my feet.

00:04:16.711 --> 00:04:19.964 align:center line:79%
And every day, whether
you think about it or not,

00:04:20.631 --> 00:04:23.801 align:center line:81%
you're deciding where to plant your feet.

00:04:25.636 --> 00:04:29.181 align:center line:79%
I had the honor and the privilege
along the way of teaching

00:04:29.181 --> 00:04:32.143 align:center line:79%
at George Washington University
for a total of nine years.

00:04:32.518 --> 00:04:33.978 align:center line:81%
Four years in the law school

00:04:34.353 --> 00:04:38.816 align:center line:79%
and five years teaching
undergraduate criminal justice.

00:04:38.816 --> 00:04:42.987 align:center line:79%
And on the first day of every semester,
I did the same thing.

00:04:43.946 --> 00:04:46.532 align:center line:81%
I would draw a brick wall.

00:04:46.574 --> 00:04:49.243 align:center line:81%
What for me, passed for a brick wall.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.038 align:center line:79%
Let me here, let me prove
I'm not a very good artist.

00:04:52.038 --> 00:04:53.748 align:center line:81%
There, there's my brick wall.

00:04:53.998 --> 00:04:57.043 align:center line:79%
I would draw it on the whiteboard
for my students,

00:04:57.918 --> 00:05:03.341 align:center line:79%
and I would tell them that brick
wall represents the rule of law,

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:09.263 align:center line:79%
specifically the first ten amendments
to the United States Constitution,

00:05:09.555 --> 00:05:14.018 align:center line:79%
the Bill of rights. And I would put
on one side of the wall the government,

00:05:14.352 --> 00:05:19.774 align:center line:79%
politicians, police, prosecutors,
and on the other side of the wall,

00:05:19.774 --> 00:05:23.486 align:center line:81%
I put us, we the people.

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:25.905 align:center line:81%
And in a very real sense,

00:05:25.905 --> 00:05:31.577 align:center line:79%
that brick wall protects
us from our own government.

00:05:31.619 --> 00:05:34.955 align:center line:79%
You know, the Bill of rights
is it's like a list of don'ts

00:05:35.748 --> 00:05:38.793 align:center line:81%
telling the government what they can't do

00:05:39.335 --> 00:05:43.464 align:center line:79%
to we the People first amendment
don't mess with our free speech rights.

00:05:44.882 --> 00:05:48.469 align:center line:79%
Fifth amendment, don't try
to make us incriminate ourselves.

00:05:49.595 --> 00:05:54.642 align:center line:79%
Sixth amendment don't mess with our right
to counsel our right to an attorney.

00:05:55.434 --> 00:05:59.397 align:center line:79%
Eighth amendment. Don't even
think about trying to inflict cruel

00:05:59.397 --> 00:06:02.858 align:center line:81%
and unusual punishment on us.

00:06:03.984 --> 00:06:06.612 align:center line:81%
That brick wall protects us all.

00:06:06.612 --> 00:06:10.491 align:center line:81%
And I do mean all American citizens.

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:12.660 align:center line:81%
Documented immigrants.

00:06:13.202 --> 00:06:15.037 align:center line:81%
Undocumented immigrants.

00:06:15.287 --> 00:06:17.665 align:center line:81%
Visitors to our nation.

00:06:17.665 --> 00:06:23.212 align:center line:79%
If your feet are on American soil,
the Constitution protects you.

00:06:24.922 --> 00:06:26.715 align:center line:81%
Now, don't get me wrong.

00:06:26.715 --> 00:06:28.926 align:center line:81%
The government, the police,

00:06:28.926 --> 00:06:32.221 align:center line:79%
the prosecutors can get
to the other side of that wall,

00:06:33.389 --> 00:06:35.224 align:center line:81%
but they've got to do it right.

00:06:35.891 --> 00:06:38.686 align:center line:81%
So you want to search my home?

00:06:39.687 --> 00:06:43.399 align:center line:79%
You better have a judicially
issued search warrant.

00:06:43.441 --> 00:06:45.025 align:center line:81%
You want to seize me?

00:06:45.025 --> 00:06:46.444 align:center line:81%
You want to arrest me?

00:06:47.278 --> 00:06:49.655 align:center line:81%
You better have an arrest warrant.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.616 align:center line:81%
So in today's America

00:06:53.659 --> 00:06:59.748 align:center line:79%
question is that brick wall
standing straight and strong?

00:07:01.292 --> 00:07:04.086 align:center line:81%
or is it beginning to weaken?

00:07:05.004 --> 00:07:06.964 align:center line:81%
Is it beginning to waver?

00:07:07.631 --> 00:07:10.426 align:center line:81%
Is it beginning to crumble even?

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:15.389 align:center line:81%
And if that wall weakens, where are we,

00:07:15.514 --> 00:07:19.226 align:center line:81%
the people going to plant our feet?

00:07:21.687 --> 00:07:25.983 align:center line:79%
Let's look at some recent
feet planting examples.

00:07:25.983 --> 00:07:30.654 align:center line:79%
And these may be familiar to you
because they've been in the news recently.

00:07:31.614 --> 00:07:38.412 align:center line:79%
In 2019, there was a young El Salvadoran
immigrant named Kilmar Abrego Garcia,

00:07:39.246 --> 00:07:42.416 align:center line:81%
who planted his feet in immigration court,

00:07:43.209 --> 00:07:46.962 align:center line:79%
and he won a court order
from an immigration judge saying

00:07:46.962 --> 00:07:51.425 align:center line:79%
that the government may not
deport him back to El Salvador

00:07:51.425 --> 00:07:56.096 align:center line:79%
because he persuaded the judge
he had a reasonable fear of persecution

00:07:56.305 --> 00:07:59.558 align:center line:81%
if he were returned to El Salvador.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:07.733 align:center line:79%
Then, sadly, horrifically,
in March of 2025,

00:08:08.108 --> 00:08:12.947 align:center line:79%
the government our government
not only violated that court order,

00:08:13.572 --> 00:08:19.954 align:center line:81%
They violated Garcia’s due process rights.

00:08:19.954 --> 00:08:24.875 align:center line:79%
in the context of this case is just
a fancy term for notice

00:08:25.459 --> 00:08:27.336 align:center line:81%
and opportunity to be heard.

00:08:28.045 --> 00:08:30.005 align:center line:81%
Notice of what the government's going

00:08:30.005 --> 00:08:33.425 align:center line:79%
to try to do to you,
like deport you to a foreign land,

00:08:33.425 --> 00:08:38.514 align:center line:79%
and an opportunity to be heard
in court by a judge to make your case,

00:08:38.514 --> 00:08:40.849 align:center line:79%
generally with the assistance
of an attorney,

00:08:40.849 --> 00:08:45.020 align:center line:79%
as to why the government
shouldn't be permitted to do that to you.

00:08:46.814 --> 00:08:51.110 align:center line:79%
But the government, our government
violated both the court order

00:08:51.318 --> 00:08:55.239 align:center line:79%
and Garcia's Fifth Amendment
due process rights.

00:08:55.823 --> 00:08:57.866 align:center line:81%
They grabbed him. They put him on a plane.

00:08:57.866 --> 00:09:00.160 align:center line:81%
They sent him to El Salvador.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:07.126 align:center line:79%
Worse, they paid El Salvador to
imprison him.

00:09:08.168 --> 00:09:11.255 align:center line:81%
in a notoriously dangerous prison.

00:09:11.255 --> 00:09:15.634 align:center line:79%
Even though Abrego Garcia
had been convicted of no crime.

00:09:18.262 --> 00:09:22.850 align:center line:79%
And as he sat in that jail cell,
he had to decide where to plant his feet.

00:09:24.018 --> 00:09:26.186 align:center line:81%
And he decided to use the rule of law

00:09:26.687 --> 00:09:29.607 align:center line:79%
and file a lawsuit
in federal court in Maryland,

00:09:29.607 --> 00:09:32.735 align:center line:79%
with the assistance
of some determined attorneys,

00:09:33.902 --> 00:09:39.158 align:center line:79%
and try to convince that judge that the
federal government should be forced

00:09:39.158 --> 00:09:41.201 align:center line:81%
to bring him back to the United States.

00:09:42.494 --> 00:09:47.333 align:center line:79%
And he won. He won. And the judge
ordered the federal government

00:09:47.333 --> 00:09:51.086 align:center line:79%
to facilitate his release
from that prison in El Salvador

00:09:51.086 --> 00:09:53.213 align:center line:81%
and return him to the United States.

00:09:53.213 --> 00:09:56.717 align:center line:79%
So his due process
rights could be honored.

00:09:58.636 --> 00:10:00.763 align:center line:81%
Government didn't like that outcome.

00:10:00.763 --> 00:10:05.142 align:center line:79%
So they appealed. And Abrego Garcia,
figuratively speaking,

00:10:05.142 --> 00:10:09.938 align:center line:79%
planted his feet in the Court
of Appeals and he won again.

00:10:10.939 --> 00:10:13.525 align:center line:81%
And the government appealed again.

00:10:13.525 --> 00:10:15.986 align:center line:81%
And Abrego Garcia, figuratively speaking,

00:10:15.986 --> 00:10:18.864 align:center line:79%
planted his feet in the United
States Supreme Court,

00:10:19.865 --> 00:10:23.994 align:center line:81%
and he won the rule of law one.

00:10:25.079 --> 00:10:27.623 align:center line:79%
And then when he was back
in the United States,

00:10:27.623 --> 00:10:32.878 align:center line:79%
he literally planted his feet back
in that federal court in Maryland.

00:10:32.878 --> 00:10:34.713 align:center line:81%
And he won a court order directing.

00:10:34.713 --> 00:10:38.175 align:center line:81%
The federal government may not deport him.

00:10:39.885 --> 00:10:44.640 align:center line:79%
That is some rule of law
driven feet planting.

00:10:47.393 --> 00:10:48.394 align:center line:81%
Another example,

00:10:50.354 --> 00:10:55.776 align:center line:79%
former DOJ paralegal
Sean Dunn through a sandwich

00:10:57.069 --> 00:10:58.487 align:center line:81%
at a police officer.

00:10:59.321 --> 00:11:02.074 align:center line:81%
You probably all saw that, right?

00:11:02.116 --> 00:11:07.246 align:center line:79%
It was captured on video and played
on an endless loop by mainstream media.

00:11:07.287 --> 00:11:12.376 align:center line:79%
An important aside,
the reason we all got to see that is

00:11:12.376 --> 00:11:16.630 align:center line:79%
because we have people all around
the country, just like you and me,

00:11:17.214 --> 00:11:21.593 align:center line:81%
Who are literally standing in the street.

00:11:21.593 --> 00:11:24.638 align:center line:79%
raising their cell phones
and recording, documenting,

00:11:24.638 --> 00:11:30.978 align:center line:79%
bearing witness to what the federal
government immigration

00:11:31.019 --> 00:11:33.689 align:center line:81%
agents are doing to we the People.

00:11:37.067 --> 00:11:39.903 align:center line:81%
And so we saw Sean Dunn get angry.

00:11:39.945 --> 00:11:43.365 align:center line:79%
He was angry. We learned
from the reporting

00:11:43.365 --> 00:11:47.870 align:center line:79%
because the government had militarized
the streets of his city, Washington,

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:52.791 align:center line:79%
D.C. he was out there protesting,
lost his cool, threw a sandwich.

00:11:54.168 --> 00:11:57.796 align:center line:79%
The sandwich, bounced off
the bulletproof vest of the officer,

00:11:58.046 --> 00:12:04.678 align:center line:79%
causing no injury
and Sean Dunne was arrested.

00:12:07.306 --> 00:12:13.270 align:center line:79%
And take it from this old prosecutor
who worked protester cases in D.C.,

00:12:13.854 --> 00:12:19.318 align:center line:79%
we have a lot of protests in D.C.,
and they can get loud,

00:12:19.651 --> 00:12:21.528 align:center line:81%
they can get enthusiastic.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:23.030 align:center line:81%
They can turn volatile.

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:25.115 align:center line:79%
People are marching.
People are protesting.

00:12:25.115 --> 00:12:26.992 align:center line:81%
They're yelling, they're chanting.

00:12:27.785 --> 00:12:29.578 align:center line:81%
Sometimes there’s pushing.

00:12:29.578 --> 00:12:33.248 align:center line:79%
People are exercising
their First Amendment rights vigorously.

00:12:34.833 --> 00:12:37.878 align:center line:79%
But not a lot of those
protesters get arrested.

00:12:38.796 --> 00:12:42.049 align:center line:81%
Some do. And when protesters get arrested,

00:12:42.049 --> 00:12:48.055 align:center line:79%
it usually results in a low level criminal
charge, what we call a misdemeanor.

00:12:48.263 --> 00:12:50.682 align:center line:79%
It's the kind of charge
that if you're convicted,

00:12:50.682 --> 00:12:52.935 align:center line:81%
a judge might order probation

00:12:52.935 --> 00:12:56.814 align:center line:79%
or might order you perform some community
service, something like that.

00:12:58.565 --> 00:13:00.526 align:center line:81%
And once Sean Dunne was arrested,

00:13:01.527 --> 00:13:05.239 align:center line:79%
the U.S. attorney for the District
of Columbia had a decision to make.

00:13:05.239 --> 00:13:06.990 align:center line:81%
What to do with Sean Dunne's case.

00:13:07.533 --> 00:13:10.035 align:center line:81%
And in my opinion, the U.S. attorney tried

00:13:10.035 --> 00:13:12.454 align:center line:81%
to push her way through that brick wall.

00:13:13.956 --> 00:13:16.917 align:center line:79%
And she sent a prosecutor
into the grand jury

00:13:18.252 --> 00:13:24.675 align:center line:79%
and had that prosecutor try to convince
the grand jury to indict,

00:13:24.675 --> 00:13:26.301 align:center line:81%
criminally indict Sean Dunne

00:13:26.301 --> 00:13:30.889 align:center line:79%
for a federal felony offense
that carries eight years in prison

00:13:32.683 --> 00:13:34.017 align:center line:81%
for tossing a sandwich.

00:13:36.603 --> 00:13:39.189 align:center line:81%
Sound like prosecutorial overreach?

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:44.111 align:center line:79%
Well, the grand jurors just
regular folks like us called from

00:13:44.111 --> 00:13:47.614 align:center line:79%
all around the city. Or the jurisdiction
in which the offense is alleged

00:13:47.614 --> 00:13:50.868 align:center line:79%
to have been committed. They sit there,
they listen to the evidence,

00:13:51.076 --> 00:13:53.996 align:center line:79%
and they serve as the conscience
of the community,

00:13:54.538 --> 00:14:00.085 align:center line:79%
and they serve as a check against
governmental abuse and An overreach

00:14:00.377 --> 00:14:05.090 align:center line:79%
and misconduct, and the grand jurors
had to decide where to plant their feet.

00:14:06.675 --> 00:14:13.307 align:center line:79%
And they planted their feet by announcing
to the prosecutor, no,

00:14:14.391 --> 00:14:20.355 align:center line:79%
we will not indict Sean Dunn
for an eight year federal felony.

00:14:20.397 --> 00:14:24.192 align:center line:79%
He could get eight years
in federal prison for tossing a sandwich.

00:14:24.192 --> 00:14:28.071 align:center line:79%
Did you ever hear the saying,
don't make a federal case out of it?

00:14:29.197 --> 00:14:32.284 align:center line:79%
It's kind of the poster child
for that case, for that saying.

00:14:33.452 --> 00:14:39.917 align:center line:79%
And they rejected the U.S.
attorney's attempt to indict Sean Dunn

00:14:39.917 --> 00:14:41.877 align:center line:81%
for that eight year federal felony.

00:14:41.877 --> 00:14:45.047 align:center line:79%
But U.S. attorney just kind
of fumbled forward and said, well,

00:14:45.047 --> 00:14:49.009 align:center line:79%
then I'm going to charge
Sean Dunn myself with a misdemeanor.

00:14:49.426 --> 00:14:53.597 align:center line:79%
And, you know, those are the cases
that are more typical and protests.

00:14:53.972 --> 00:14:57.976 align:center line:79%
And you should know you don't need a grand
jury indictment to charge somebody

00:14:57.976 --> 00:15:00.646 align:center line:81%
with a misdemeanor, only with a felony.

00:15:00.646 --> 00:15:01.647 align:center line:81%
So,

00:15:02.105 --> 00:15:04.650 align:center line:79%
you know, prosecutors
signed the criminal complaint.

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:09.488 align:center line:79%
That's all it takes. And now Sean Dunn
has to make another decision where

00:15:09.488 --> 00:15:12.574 align:center line:79%
to plant his feet. Does he demand
his right to a jury trial,

00:15:12.574 --> 00:15:15.953 align:center line:81%
or does he cry uncle and plead guilty?

00:15:15.953 --> 00:15:19.164 align:center line:81%
Well, he demanded a jury trial.

00:15:19.498 --> 00:15:24.461 align:center line:79%
And now we have another
group of citizens sitting

00:15:24.461 --> 00:15:29.341 align:center line:79%
as the conscience of the community.
This time it's 12 in a wooden box

00:15:29.341 --> 00:15:32.052 align:center line:81%
in a courtroom in Washington, DC.

00:15:33.136 --> 00:15:37.891 align:center line:79%
Who listened to the evidence
from the prosecution,

00:15:38.183 --> 00:15:43.271 align:center line:79%
listened to the evidence from
Sean Dunn's attorney,

00:15:44.481 --> 00:15:47.567 align:center line:81%
and they planted their feet by announcing

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:51.989 align:center line:81%
that the verdict was not guilty.

00:15:53.699 --> 00:15:56.451 align:center line:81%
That is some important feet planting.

00:15:58.036 --> 00:16:02.624 align:center line:79%
And indeed, we've had a lot
of important feet planting recently

00:16:03.208 --> 00:16:07.087 align:center line:79%
that that young El Salvadoran
immigrant, Abrego Garcia,

00:16:07.129 --> 00:16:12.676 align:center line:79%
that former DOJ paralegal
Sean Dunn, the grand jurors,

00:16:12.968 --> 00:16:15.595 align:center line:81%
the trial jurors, the folks

00:16:15.595 --> 00:16:18.473 align:center line:81%
who are standing firm across the country

00:16:18.473 --> 00:16:20.559 align:center line:79%
and using their cell
phones to document what

00:16:20.559 --> 00:16:23.395 align:center line:81%
the government is doing to the people.

00:16:25.355 --> 00:16:32.154 align:center line:79%
And we, you and I,
make rule of law driven feet

00:16:32.154 --> 00:16:35.240 align:center line:81%
planting decisions every day.

00:16:37.325 --> 00:16:43.498 align:center line:79%
But the decisions that we make
usually involve things like speeding,

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:47.502 align:center line:79%
stopping at stop signs,
paying for parking.

00:16:47.502 --> 00:16:49.046 align:center line:81%
But in today's America,

00:16:49.796 --> 00:16:54.217 align:center line:79%
we have far more consequential
rule of law driven feet

00:16:54.259 --> 00:16:56.803 align:center line:81%
planting decisions to make.

00:16:59.056 --> 00:17:02.059 align:center line:81%
So when the time comes

00:17:03.226 --> 00:17:10.233 align:center line:79%
and the issues involve
things like the health

00:17:10.233 --> 00:17:14.780 align:center line:79%
of American democracy,
maybe even the viability,

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:21.703 align:center line:79%
the survival of American democracy,
when the time comes, the question is,

00:17:22.996 --> 00:17:25.665 align:center line:81%
where will you plant your feet?

00:17:27.709 --> 00:17:31.254 align:center line:81%
And regarding when that time might come,

00:17:32.672 --> 00:17:33.673 align:center line:81%
the way I see it,

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:37.677 align:center line:81%
It’s time. Thank you.
